---
import Cta from "../components/Cta.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="CRM and automation"
  description="CRM setup, lead management, enquiry tracking, and practical workflow automation. Custom-built platforms and complex integrations are not standard packages."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="CRM and automation"
    title="Organise the leads you already have, then stop repeating the same steps."
    lede="CRM solutions and business automation are separate kinds of work, often used together. We configure practical tools and the workflows we agree. We do not ship a custom-built CRM platform or an AI product as a standard package."
  />

  <section class="section anchor" id="crm" aria-labelledby="crm-heading">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2 id="crm-heading">CRM solutions</h2>
        <p>
          This is setup and configuration, not a product we invent. We organise a CRM around the way you handle
          enquiries: the fields you need, the stages a lead moves through, and a shared list your team can open.
        </p>
        <ul class="plain-list">
          <li>CRM setup and configuration</li>
          <li>Lead management and enquiry tracking</li>
          <li>A customer database with the details you actually use</li>
          <li>Sales pipeline organisation, using stages that match your work</li>
          <li>Straightforward business integrations, such as a form writing into the CRM</li>
          <li>Internal views and lists inside that CRM, so people are not building their own spreadsheets</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <h2>What this is not</h2>
        <p>
          A standard CRM engagement does not include a custom-built CRM platform, a bespoke analytics product, or a
          promise that the pipeline will produce a certain amount of revenue.
        </p>
        <p>If you need software written from scratch, that is a different project and we will scope it on its own.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section anchor" id="automation" aria-labelledby="automation-heading">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2 id="automation-heading">Business automation</h2>
        <p>
          Automation here means a defined workflow: something that happens the same way each time, without someone
          retyping it. We configure that workflow. We do not leave it open-ended.
        </p>
        <ul class="plain-list">
          <li>Automated lead capture from a website or form</li>
          <li>Email notifications when a new enquiry arrives</li>
          <li>Follow-up workflows so a quiet lead is not forgotten</li>
          <li>Form-to-CRM, so the message and the record are the same event</li>
          <li>Appointment or enquiry routing, where the tool you use supports it</li>
          <li>Data sync between the systems named in the scope</li>
          <li>Custom workflow automation for one agreed process, not a general automation platform</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <h2>Possible later, not included by default</h2>
        <p>
          Complex integrations across many systems, custom code between tools that do not already connect, and AI
          products are outside a standard package. They can be discussed as future work with their own scope. They are
          not assumed when you ask for lead capture or a follow-up email.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>How the two work together</h2>
      <p>
        A form on the website creates a lead. The CRM holds it in the right stage. A notification tells someone, and a
        follow-up rule reminds them if nothing happens. That sequence is the usual pairing. Either part can also be
        done on its own.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/web-development">See website development</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Cta
    heading="Want the enquiries in one place?"
    text="Describe how a new message is handled today. We will say whether a CRM setup, a workflow, or both is the practical next step."
  />
</BaseLayout>
